{
 "_comment": "Accepted by the user, 20 September 2026. The six conditions (RULES.md rule 1), the PubMed search words (rule 2) and the ranked score lists (rule 5). Scores are ranked: clinician-rated first, then a questionnaire made for the one condition, then a part of a mixed questionnaire. This file round-trips through json.dump(indent=2). Updated 20 September 2026 after the pilot: validated short forms count as the parent score and are listed in its aliases; child scores added to sleep and cognition. Updated 21 September 2026 after wave 2: added the child scores CDI, SCARED and SCAS; the Zung SDS and SAS; the POMS total mood disturbance; and the PANAS. Each sits by rule 5's order, so a clinician-rated score still outranks a self-rated one and a mixed questionnaire still comes last. Corrected the same day: the PANAS entry is the negative affect scale only. PANAS has no total score, and on its positive affect scale a good result is a HIGHER score, which this condition would have read as harm. A paper reporting only positive affect is instrument_not_listed. Updated 18 October 2026 under rule 5's admission test: added PAS, PRAS-ASD, ASC-ASD, the Goldberg scale's two scores and the CBCL anxiety problems scale (anxiety); the GDS, PROMIS depression (depression); the Levenstein PSQ (felt-stress); ESS and PDSS (sleep); PHES and the Mullen composite (cognition). Refusals are listed in notes/score-admissions.md.",
